{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Lest they cause you to sin against Me.</b> Here the Master revealed that the deficiency touches the Creator. The intellectual implication of the matter is that Israel, being of the aspect of holiness, when they serve idolatrous worship — behold, they diminish from the scale of holiness and are lacking from their root, and thus the deficiency is found to touch the very root of holiness." "<b>For it will be a snare to you,</b> etc. Meaning, He gave a reason: from where would it enter the mind that Israel would be suspected of this — to exchange their glory for that which does not profit? Therefore He informed them that idolatrous worship misleads its worshippers to become ensnared after it, as they of blessed memory said (Avodah Zarah 55a) that there is a form of idolatrous worship that reveals hidden things and treasures and foretells the future, and therefore HaShem was protective of His children lest they become ensnared."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:06.120097533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}